  "tip": "TIP",
  "tips": "Helpful Tips",
  "tips_company": "Configure your organization's basic information including name, address, tax ID, and contact details. This information appears on exported documents, invoices, and official reports. Keep this up-to-date to ensure accurate document processing and professional correspondence.",
  "tips_dashboard": "Customize your dashboard view with widgets, filters, and data visualizations. Configure which metrics and KPIs are displayed for different user roles. A well-configured dashboard provides instant insights into document processing performance.",
  "tips_default": "This setting helps you configure an important aspect of DocBits. Proper configuration ensures optimal performance and seamless integration with your workflows. Check the documentation for detailed setup instructions.",
  "tips_document_types": "Define and configure document types like invoices, purchase orders, and delivery notes. Set up extraction fields, validation rules, and approval workflows for each type. Proper configuration ensures accurate data extraction and efficient processing.",
  "tips_email_ingestion": "Set up automated document import from email accounts with smart filtering and routing. Configure sender whitelists, subject line rules, and attachment processing. Email ingestion eliminates manual forwarding and speeds up processing.",
  "tips_email_templates": "Customize email templates for notifications, alerts, and automated communications. Use variables to personalize messages with document data and user information. Professional templates improve communication and brand consistency.",
  "tips_export": "Set up automated export of processed documents and extracted data to your ERP, accounting system, or archive. Configure export formats, mapping rules, and scheduling. Automated export ensures seamless data flow to downstream systems.",
  "tips_groups_users_permissions": "Configure groups, their users, and permissions for different document types. Control access levels and workflow capabilities for each user group. Use this to implement role-based access control across your organization.",
  "tips_import": "Configure automated document import from email, FTP, cloud storage, and other sources. Set up import rules, file naming conventions, and processing triggers. Automated import eliminates manual upload and accelerates document processing.",
  "tips_integration": "Connect DocBits with your ERP, CRM, and other business systems using API keys and webhooks. Seamless integration enables automated data exchange, reduces manual entry, and ensures real-time updates. Configure integrations to streamline your document workflows.",
  "tips_list_of_values": "Define dropdown lists and validation values for document fields. Set up currency codes, payment terms, tax codes, and custom lookup lists. Controlled values improve data quality and user input efficiency.",
  "tips_ocr_settings": "Configure OCR engine settings, language packs, and image pre-processing options. Optimize recognition accuracy for different document formats and quality levels. Proper OCR configuration is critical for accurate data extraction.",
  "tips_roles_groups": "Define user roles with specific permissions and capabilities for document processing workflows. Create role templates and assign them to user groups. Role-based access ensures security while maintaining operational efficiency.",
  "tips_rule_management": "Create and manage business rules for document validation, approval routing, and data processing. Set up conditional logic, tolerance ranges, and automated actions. Smart rules reduce manual intervention and improve accuracy.",
  "tips_sub_organizations": "Create and manage sub-organizations for departments, branches, or separate business units. Each sub-organization can have its own settings, users, and document workflows. This enables multi-tenant document processing within a single DocBits instance.",
  "tips_users": "Manage user accounts, roles, and access permissions for your organization. Create new users, assign admin rights, and control who can access specific features and documents. Proper user management ensures security and maintains system integrity.",
